# ClaudeSwitch — the single source of truth for the VISIBLE version
# (CFBundleShortVersionString) of each update channel.
#
# Sources/ClaudeSwitchCore/AppVersion.swift is a stamped mirror of whichever
# line the build used; it decides nothing. The monotonic CFBundleVersion build
# number is separate, lives in Info.plist, and is what Sparkle actually compares
# when deciding whether a feed item is newer.
#
# Invariant, enforced by scripts/version-plan.sh: Beta is always at or ahead of
# Stable. Both channels are served by ONE build and ONE appcast — beta items
# carry <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>, stable items carry no channel
# tag at all (that is Sparkle 2's semantics, not a shortcut).
#
# A stable release is TWO publishes, in this order:
#   ./scripts/build-dmg.sh --beta   --publish   # bumps BETA past the lead
#   ...soak it...
#   ./scripts/build-dmg.sh --stable --publish   # promotes STABLE to that lead
#
# These lines are rewritten by build-dmg.sh after a successful publish. Don't
# hand-edit them mid-release.
#
# Product facts (each app in the family has its OWN, never shared):
#   bundle id : com.irvcassio.ClaudeSwitch
#   feed      : https://www.doppoworks.com/downloads/claudeswitch/appcast.xml
#   keypair   : EdDSA, generated on the build machine and kept there. The
#               private half is an exported FILE, referenced by PATH from
#               scripts/signing.env (SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY) and passed to
#               sign_update -f. It is never committed, never inlined, and
#               never copied off that machine — so keypair generation and
#               every --publish happen on the build machine only.
#
STABLE=1.0.2
BETA=1.0.2
